Druski is hosting Saturday Night Live for the first time this weekend, while The Strokes will be the musical guest for a fourth time. They made their SNL debut in January 2002 and also performed in 2006 and 2011. The band is promoting their most recently released album, July&#8217;s Reality Awaits , which debuted at No. 13 on the all-genre Billboard 200 and at No. 5 on the Top Rock & Alternative Albums chart.

Saturday Night Live  airs at 11:30 p.m. ET/8:30 p.m. PT on NBC and streams on Peacock. ( See all the options to watch  SNL  here.)
